.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-chat-add-member - Add one or more members to a chat


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams chat add-member   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add members to a chat. Each one is added with the documented owner role: a
guest role is a tenant decision, and \fBmember\fR is not accepted in the delegated
flow (refs/graph/api-reference/v1.0/api/chat-post.md:47).

.PP
Every member is attempted, so one failure does not hide the others; the
command exits 1 when any of them failed.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the Graph requests without sending them

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add-member


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-chat(1)\fP
